===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|jǫkull|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|jekulaz|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|jikilaz|lang=gem-pro}}. Diminutive of {{term|jaki||a piece of ice, broken ice|lang=non}}.<ref>[http://web.ff.cuni.cz/cgi-bin/uaa_slovnik/gmc_search_v3?cmd=viewthis&id=cv:b0327:35 JÖKULL] from Cleasby/Vigfusson</ref><ref name="da">[http://ordnet.dk/ddo/ordbog?query=j%C3%B8kel jøkel substantiv, fælleskøn]</ref>

